  "title": "Unified title",
  "summary": "The Supreme Court dismissed a plea against the Delhi Metro, Delhi Police, and Union Home Secretary for violating the court's October 9 order to prevent a complete ban on metro and train services during the CJP protest. The court also ruled against influencers for jokes related to the riots.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Supreme Court dismissed a plea against the Delhi Metro, Delhi Police, and Union Home Secretary for violating the court's October 9 order to prevent a complete ban on metro and train services during the CJP protest.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The court also ruled against influencers for jokes related to the riots.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The plea referred to the apex court's October 9 order, which was passed while hearing a separate petition against the closure of 57 metro stations and cancellation of trains to Delhi in view of the protest.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
