    {
      "title": "Delhi protests: SC to hear contempt plea against authorities on Sunday",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/delhi-protests-sc-to-hear-contempt-plea-against-authorities-on-sunday-126101000873_1.html",
      "description": "The Supreme Court will hear on Sunday a plea seeking initiation of contempt proceedings against authorities for alleged blatant violation of the court's direction to ensure no complete prohibition on metro and trains services in Delhi due to the CJP protest.\nAccording to the cause list of October 11 uploaded on the apex court website, the plea would come up for hearing before a bench of justices Joymalya Bagchi and V Mohana.\nThe plea, filed by advocate Shailendra Mani Tripathi, has arrayed Union Home Secretary Govind Mohan, Delhi Police Commissioner Anurag Kumar and Delhi Metro Rail Corporation chairperson D Thara as respondents.\n\"This brutal assault on the fundamental rights of the citizens and sheer disregard to the orders of this court amounts to deliberate, intentional attempt on the part of Delhi Metro, Delhi Police and the Union government which must be dealt with an iron hand,\" the plea, filed through advocate Chand Qureshi, said.\nThe petition referred to the top court's ...",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-10T15:53:36"
    },
    {
      "title": "CJP protest: Plea seeks contempt action over alleged SC order violation",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/cjp-protest-plea-seeks-contempt-action-over-alleged-sc-order-violation-126101000248_1.html",
      "description": "A plea was filed in the Supreme Court on Saturday seeking initiation of contempt proceedings against the authorities alleging violation of the apex court's direction to ensure no complete prohibition of movement of metro and trains operated by Indian Railways here on October 10 due to the CJP protest.\nThe petition, filed by Shailendra Mani Tripathi, has arrayed Union Home Secretary Govind Mohan and other as party respondents.\nThe plea alleged that authorities have continued with the closure of metro stations in the national capital despite the top court's October 9 direction.\nIt said these restrictions have crippled public life and caused hardships to the public.\nThe petition has referred to the apex court's October 9 order, which was passed while hearing a separate petition against the closure of 57 metro stations and cancellation of trains to Delhi in view of the protest.\nThe protest call has been given by the Cockroach Janta Party (CJP)  against Chief Election Commissioner Gyan",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-10T08:39:58"
    }
  ]
